1. Scope

The "Software" means the original application code, scripts, documentation,
and original catalog descriptions in this repository, to the extent that
their copyright holders have made them available under this license.
"Licensor" means each such copyright holder. Third-party materials described
in section 5 are not part of the Software.

2. Permission

Subject to these terms, the Licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive license to use, copy, study, and modify the Software for your
own personal use and for shared personal or educational use within a closed
private group. You may run original or modified versions on your devices
or on a server, including rented infrastructure, provided access to the
running application is restricted to you or that group. There are no
restrictions on the changes you may make for these permitted uses.

A closed private group is a defined circle of people connected independently
of the hosted application, such as friends, family, classmates, or members
of a particular school class or study group. Access must be limited to those
people through accounts, privately shared credentials, a private network,
or equivalent access controls. An unlisted URL alone is not sufficient.
Membership must not be offered to the general public. Operating a service
for customers or recruiting otherwise unrelated users into an invitation-only
group does not qualify. Group members may join or leave without changing
the group's private character.

You may share the Software's source code, including modified source code
and public repository forks. Shared copies must include this license and
retain copyright and third-party notices. You must identify modifications
you distribute. Recipients receive permission to use the covered Software
under this license directly from the Licensor. You may not relicense the
covered Software in a way that removes these restrictions.

3. No public hosting or competing services

You may not deploy, host, or otherwise make a running version of the Software
publicly accessible, or provide its functionality to the public through
another application or service. This restriction applies to original and
modified versions, including static builds, public previews, mirrors, and
versions embedded in other websites. It applies whether access is free,
paid, commercial, educational, or otherwise noncommercial.

A service is publicly accessible if members of the public can obtain access,
including through open registration, payment, or publicly distributed
credentials. Credentials shared only within a closed private group are
permitted under section 2.

You may not use the Software to operate or offer a competing hosted service.
For this license, that means a service offering the Software's exam browsing,
search, or related functionality to users outside a closed private group,
including a service that limits access to selected customers or invitees.
Permitted personal and closed-group use is not competition merely because
its users choose that instance instead of the Licensor's website.

Publishing source code for inspection or download as permitted by section 2
is not public hosting or operation of a competing service.

